invariant: INV-16
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: table_select leaves its scan once it has passed the entry its
  index names, so how many entries a step reads is the digit of the
  private exponent it is on. Every byte still comes out the same, so the
  vectors and the equivalence test pass, and the pinned clang emits as
  many conditional branches as before on both 64-bit specs, so the
  branch count passes too. inv-16-rsa-table-read refuses an if or a break
  inside table_select.

--- old
        for (size_t i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            o[i] = (o[i] & ~mask) | (table->powers[entry][i] & mask);
        }
--- new
        for (size_t i = 0; i < k; i++) {
            o[i] = (o[i] & ~mask) | (table->powers[entry][i] & mask);
        }
        if (entry == index) {
            break;
        }
